  "details": "As a sort of low data mode, the further away a player is from the user, said user recieves fewer and fewer packets from the player as the distance increases. it should also be customisable distance also. Implementation would also be rather simple, and to compensate for the increased stutter of lower packets the smoothing algorithm for movements can scale equal to the reduction of information. this would in turn reduce network load for users with poor connection and allow for smoother play albeit testing will be needed as to the extent of the improvement, but an improvement nonetheless.",
